;; Wasmtime, and one component run under grants the image states.
;;
;; The grants are the appliance's security policy and they live in
;; /etc/default/wasm-component as wasmtime CLI flags. That is not a
;; workaround: wasmtime denies by default, and every flag is a widening.
;; As of wasmtime 48 the runtime's own default configuration denies creating
;; TCP and UDP sockets, and filesystem permissions are per-directory and
;; either read-only or read-write.
;;
;; Because the file is carried with path-append, its contents are in the
;; solution hash. So "this image grants read access to one directory and no
;; network" is content-addressed, and an image whose grants were widened is a
;; different image by identity, not just by content.

(fragment feature:wasm-runtime

  (doc "Wasmtime plus a component, run under explicit grants")

  (requires
    (capability mmu)
    (capability glibc)        ; the release binaries link against glibc
    (capability systemd-init))

  (buildroot
    (y BR2_PACKAGE_WASMTIME)

    ;; The runtime's configuration, the unit, the component, and the symlink
    ;; that enables it.
    (path-append BR2_ROOTFS_OVERLAY "files")))
